  "linked_method": "Read actual native ELF objdump -d -r --demangle and llvm-nm-21 --print-size --numeric-sort --demangle. Counts stop at exact ELF symbol end, retain in-body padding and all branches including untimed zero-query specializations; they are static facts, not modeled cycles.",
  "observations": [
    "All 81 paired-median direct/construct ratios improve by at least5%. Generic preparation includes a real prepare_packet_read call once per block on all three profiles; direct and shared routes do not call it.",
    "Against shared-prepared plans no x86 paired-median case loses5%; ARM has nine wins at q1 and twelve losses at q8/q64. The twelve losses are all nine q64 cells and three tight q8 cells. Retain both results; direct binding does not dominate shared reuse.",
    "ARM and AVX512 routes call the exact same out-of-line predicate<...,16>::filter<greater_equal> symbol in their respective ELF. AVX2 inlines filtering into each route, hoists mask/strided address work and has no successful-path call in shared/direct traverse.",
    "ARM shared/direct query loops at0xdd60..0xddc0 and0xdf40..0xdfa0 have the same 25-mnemonic sequence, with changed registers/operands and stack placements. Shared reserves 224 stack bytes, direct 208. Predicate sits atsp+64 vs sp+48; view atsp+80 vs sp+64. These facts do not causally explain theARM reused-query timing losses.",
    "Direct traverse is larger than shared on all three profiles partly because it separates a zero-query traversal, absent from timedq1/q8/q64. Whole-function byte/instruction counts are not repeated-query work counts.",
    "AVX2 shared/direct reserve296/280 bytes after six pushes; AVX-512 136/120 after six pushes. Generic-plan routes align stack to64 and reserve0xc80 (AVX2),0x840 (AVX512), or0x7e0 plus96 saved bytes before alignment(ARM). A smaller emitted frame does not establish allocator-class or complete resident-memory savings."
  ],
